/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig

# Go interop harness build output. `go build ./cmd/gen` writes the binary into the
# working directory, so these are easy to commit by accident — and they must not be,
# for a licensing reason rather than a tidiness one: they link katie, so a committed
# binary would make this repository distribute an AGPL derivative work. The whole
# point of keeping upstream/ as submodules is that this repository ships none of that
# code. See docs/licensing.md.
/interop/go/gen
/interop/go/verify
/interop/go/bin/
/interop/go/*.test

# local scratch — never committed
/.scratch/

# Generated evidence page. Built by CI and deployed to GitHub Pages, never
# committed: a checked-in copy would be a second source of truth for results that
# are only meaningful as the output of a test run.
/site/
